 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Look in `src/tessel/cli.py`, because that's where `tessel run` discovers the app.\n\n- **`find_best_app` (around line 67):** it looks for `app`/`application` and then falls back to the `create_app` and `make_app` factories. It calls the factory with no arguments, so a required `config_name` raises a `TypeError` and the lookup fails.\n- **`locate_app` (around line 230) and `ScriptInfo.load_app` (around line 341):** these are the callers that resolve `--app` and import the module.\n- **The `--app` help text (around line 459):** it says the value can be `name(args)`. This is likely your fix.\n\nTwo ways to fix it, without touching the CLI:\n\n1. Pass the argument explicitly: `tessel --app 'yourmodule:create_app(\"development\")' run`.\n2. Give the argument a default: `def create_app(config_name=None)`. Alternatively, expose a module-level `app` or a zero-argument `make_app()` wrapper that calls `create_app(\"development\")`.\n\nI haven't confirmed the call path beyond the grep hits, so check `find_best_app` to see how it handles the `TypeError`.",
